  "worked_solution": "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $162+108+72+48+\u22ef$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{108}{162} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $1-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{27}{64}+\u22ef$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{4})}{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $-10-9-8.1-7.29-\u22ef$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{-9}{-10} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\nIn conclusion, series I, II, and III converge.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
